From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: xpon: fold the GEM port counters in before the session
 stop

gpon_disable() cleared mac_enabled before gpon_clear_hw_tables(), so the
accumulate that runs when the GEM table changes returned early and the
counts since the last poll (up to a minute) were dropped when the slots
were freed. With gpon_stop_clear_gems on by default (999-67) that
happens on every session stop, and ME 341 under-reported the 15-minute
interval holding the restart. Accumulate first, while the MAC runs.

Found in a review of 999-58..67.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_xpon.c
@@ -3970,6 +3970,18 @@ static void gpon_disable(struct xpon_pri
 		gpon_read(priv, GPON_INT_STATUS));
 
 	/*
+	 * Fold the per-GEM MIB in while the MAC still runs: the stop clears
+	 * the GEM table and the rows are reassigned on the next session, so
+	 * the last poll window (up to a minute) would be lost from ME 341.
+	 */
+	if (mac_enabled) {
+		mutex_lock(&priv->gem_mib_lock);
+		if (priv->gem_mib_enabled)
+			gpon_mib_accumulate_locked(priv);
+		mutex_unlock(&priv->gem_mib_lock);
+	}
+
+	/*
 	 * Mask the MAC before cancelling queued FSM work. The Linux IRQ line
 	 * remains enabled so no activation edge is lost across a restart.
 	 */
